hvm5bis

hvm5bis is a port of HVM4 (https://github.com/HigherOrderCO/HVM4) to
Bend 2 (https://github.com/bendlang/bend). It is made from HVM4 at commit
6defdfc7dae2a3cca5dd6e74ed0612385b5646a8 ("collapse: general filter-credit
scheduler for -C search ordering", 2026-05-29): its src/hvm.c (the
runtime, parser, printer and collapser) is translated from C to Bend, and
its tests (devs/test) and benchmarks (devs/bench) are run against it.

HVM4 was created by Victor Taelin (victortaelin) and is developed by
HigherOrderCO and HVM4's contributors. Every algorithm, interaction rule,
syntax and test in hvm5bis is theirs; the Bend code is a translation of it.

License. HVM4's repository has no LICENSE file, and GitHub reports no
license for it (licenseInfo: null) at the commit above. No license is
claimed here for HVM4's code or for this translation of it; hvm5bis adds
no LICENSE file until that is settled with HigherOrderCO.

Bend is HigherOrderCO's, created by Victor Taelin, licensed under the
Apache License, Version 2.0; hvm5bis is written in it and built with it
(Bend 2.0.39).
